WEBVTT

00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:26.039
Back in 1835, Samuel
Colt made a special gun.

00:03:26.089 --> 00:03:28.189
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:03:35.289 --> 00:03:37.489
The Colt is gone, and it
seems pretty damn likely

00:03:37.589 --> 00:03:39.089
That the demon is behind all of this.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.189
Whoops.

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:46.089
Crossroads are where pacts are made.

00:03:46.289 --> 00:03:47.789
In selling your soul, rituals like this,

00:03:47.889 --> 00:03:49.489
You got to put your own
photo into the mix, right?

00:03:49.589 --> 00:03:51.989
I know all about you, Dean Winchester.

00:03:52.189 --> 00:03:55.089
I'm looking for the best and brightest.

00:03:55.189 --> 00:03:56.489
I'm Sam. I'm Jake.

00:03:56.589 --> 00:03:58.189
This is a competition.

00:03:58.489 --> 00:04:01.289
Only one of you crazy kids

00:04:01.389 --> 00:04:02.989
Is gonna make it out of here alive.

00:04:03.089 --> 00:04:04.089
Unh!

00:04:05.489 --> 00:04:08.889
You're tough, you're
smart, you're well-Trained.

00:04:08.989 --> 00:04:10.639
Sam, you're my favorite.

00:04:10.689 --> 00:04:12.289
Sam! Dean!

00:04:12.489 --> 00:04:13.589
Sam, look out!

00:04:14.289 --> 00:04:15.089
Unh!

00:04:15.189 --> 00:04:16.289
No!

00:04:30.189 --> 00:04:31.489
Sam!!

00:04:49.089 --> 00:04:49.789
Dean?

00:04:54.289 --> 00:04:55.389
Brought you this back.

00:05:00.189 --> 00:05:01.389
No, thanks. I'm fine.

00:05:03.689 --> 00:05:04.689
You should eat something.

00:05:06.189 --> 00:05:07.289
I said I'm fine.

00:05:18.789 --> 00:05:19.389
Dean...

00:05:20.589 --> 00:05:22.489
I hate to bring this up. I really do.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.089
But don't you think maybe it's time...

00:05:25.989 --> 00:05:27.289
We bury Sam?

00:05:30.189 --> 00:05:30.989
No.

00:05:35.989 --> 00:05:37.539
We could maybe...

00:05:37.589 --> 00:05:39.589
What -- Torch
his corpse?

00:05:41.689 --> 00:05:42.489
Not yet.

00:05:45.689 --> 00:05:47.489
I want you to come with me.

00:05:48.089 --> 00:05:49.489
I'm not going anywhere.

00:05:50.689 --> 00:05:51.989
Dean, please.

00:05:52.089 --> 00:05:53.689
Won't you cut me some slack?

00:05:54.489 --> 00:05:56.689
I just don't think you
should be alone, that's all.

00:05:58.389 --> 00:06:00.489
I got to admit -- I
could use your help.

00:06:01.589 --> 00:06:03.489
Something big
is going down --

00:06:04.689 --> 00:06:06.089
End-Of-The-World
big.

00:06:06.189 --> 00:06:07.439
Well, then let it end!

00:06:09.389 --> 00:06:10.589
You don't mean that.

00:06:12.489 --> 00:06:13.389
You don't think so?

00:06:15.689 --> 00:06:16.189
Huh?

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:18.189
You don't think I've given enough?

00:06:20.389 --> 00:06:21.689
You don't think I've paid enough?

00:06:23.489 --> 00:06:24.389
I'm done with it.

00:06:25.789 --> 00:06:26.889
All of it.

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:30.489
And if you know what's good for you,

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:32.189
Turn around and get
the hell out of here.

00:06:35.589 --> 00:06:36.489
Go!!

00:06:45.289 --> 00:06:46.089
I'm sorry.

00:06:50.789 --> 00:06:51.689
I'm sorry.

00:06:52.789 --> 00:06:53.889
Please just go.

00:07:04.189 --> 00:07:05.489
You know where I'll be.

00:07:43.189 --> 00:07:43.989
Howdy, Jake.

00:07:48.489 --> 00:07:50.089
I'm -- I'm
dreaming, aren't I?

00:07:51.689 --> 00:07:53.689
I got a genius on my hands.

00:07:55.789 --> 00:07:57.689
Well, congratulations, Jake.

00:07:57.789 --> 00:07:59.689
You're it --
Last man standing.

00:08:00.689 --> 00:08:01.889
The american idol.

00:08:02.589 --> 00:08:03.189
I have to
admit --

00:08:03.289 --> 00:08:05.389
You weren't the horse I was betting on,

00:08:05.489 --> 00:08:08.189
But still, I got to give it to you.

00:08:08.289 --> 00:08:10.689
Go... to hell.

00:08:11.489 --> 00:08:13.789
Been there, done that.

00:08:13.989 --> 00:08:15.589
Everything you
put me through --

00:08:15.989 --> 00:08:17.589
Dragging me to that place,

00:08:17.989 --> 00:08:19.189
Making me kill those people...

00:08:19.289 --> 00:08:21.189
All part of the beauty pageant.

00:08:22.489 --> 00:08:25.389
Jake, I needed the
strongest, and that's you.

00:08:25.789 --> 00:08:26.989
Needed me for what?

00:08:27.089 --> 00:08:29.989
Oh, I got a laundry list
of tasty things for you.

00:08:30.089 --> 00:08:31.989
The only thing I'm gonna do

00:08:32.389 --> 00:08:34.889
Is wake up, hunt you down,

00:08:35.089 --> 00:08:36.788
And kill you myself.

00:08:36.889 --> 00:08:38.788
You know, others have tried.

00:08:39.989 --> 00:08:41.189
It's not easy.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:46.288
Trust me, Jake. You want to
be a good little soldier here.

00:08:46.489 --> 00:08:47.788
And if I'm not?

00:08:48.288 --> 00:08:50.089
If you're a bad little soldier,

00:08:50.788 --> 00:08:53.288
Well, that dear old mom of yours,

00:08:53.589 --> 00:08:56.589
That adorable little sister...

00:08:57.189 --> 00:09:00.989
I'll make certain that
they both live long enough

00:09:01.288 --> 00:09:03.288
To know the chewy taste

00:09:03.788 --> 00:09:05.788
Of their own intestines.

00:09:08.989 --> 00:09:10.288
No, Jake.

00:09:10.489 --> 00:09:11.589
I'm not bluffing.

00:09:18.389 --> 00:09:19.889
What do you want me to do?

00:09:20.288 --> 00:09:22.589
Like I said
-- Genius.

00:09:35.389 --> 00:09:36.589
You know, when
we were little --

00:09:38.389 --> 00:09:40.189
You couldn't have
been more than 5 --

00:09:41.989 --> 00:09:44.089
You just started asking questions.

00:09:47.889 --> 00:09:49.689
How come we didn't have a mom?

00:09:51.288 --> 00:09:53.089
Why do we always have to move around?

00:09:54.189 --> 00:09:55.288
Where'd dad go

00:09:55.788 --> 00:09:58.389
When he'd take off for days at a time?

00:09:59.489 --> 00:10:01.989
I remember I begged you
-- "Quit asking, Sammy.

00:10:02.989 --> 00:10:04.389
Man, you don't want to know."

00:10:07.189 --> 00:10:08.989
I just wanted you to be a kid...

00:10:10.589 --> 00:10:11.989
Just for a little while longer.

00:10:16.288 --> 00:10:17.889
I always tried to protect you

00:10:21.389 --> 00:10:22.589
Keep you safe.

00:10:27.389 --> 00:10:29.089
Dad didn't even have to tell me.

00:10:31.489 --> 00:10:33.889
It was just always my
responsibility, you know?

00:10:37.288 --> 00:10:38.788
It's like I had one job...

00:10:40.788 --> 00:10:41.889
I had one job...

00:10:44.089 --> 00:10:45.489
And I screwed it up.

00:10:51.288 --> 00:10:52.189
I blew it.

00:10:55.788 --> 00:10:57.089
And for that, I'm sorry.

00:11:04.989 --> 00:11:06.489
I guess that's what I do.

00:11:08.189 --> 00:11:10.089
I let down the people I love.

00:11:12.089 --> 00:11:13.589
I let dad down.

00:11:18.589 --> 00:11:20.889
And now I guess I'm just
supposed to let you down, too.

00:11:25.689 --> 00:11:26.788
How can I?

00:11:29.288 --> 00:11:30.889
How am I supposed to live with that?

00:11:33.589 --> 00:11:34.989
What am I supposed to do?

00:11:36.589 --> 00:11:37.489
Sammy.

00:11:40.989 --> 00:11:41.788
God.

00:11:45.788 --> 00:11:47.689
What am I supposed to do?

00:11:55.389 --> 00:11:57.288
What am I supposed to do?!

00:13:02.989 --> 00:13:04.089
Come on, already.

00:13:04.589 --> 00:13:06.288
Show your face, you bitch!

00:13:08.089 --> 00:13:10.389
Easy, sugar. You'll wake the neighbors.

00:13:18.189 --> 00:13:18.889
Dean.

00:13:19.889 --> 00:13:22.489
It is so, so good to see you.

00:13:24.889 --> 00:13:26.889
I mean it. Look at you.

00:13:27.489 --> 00:13:30.889
Gone and got your family
killed, all alone in the world.

00:13:31.889 --> 00:13:33.288
It's too sweet.

00:13:36.288 --> 00:13:38.489
Excuse me. You're gonna
have to give me a moment.

00:13:38.589 --> 00:13:40.889
Sometimes you got to
stop and smell the roses.

00:13:41.689 --> 00:13:43.389
I should send you straight back to hell.

00:13:43.489 --> 00:13:44.889
Oh, you should.

00:13:45.389 --> 00:13:46.489
But you won't.

00:13:49.089 --> 00:13:50.288
And I know why.

00:13:51.589 --> 00:13:53.189
Oh, yeah? Yeah.

00:13:53.889 --> 00:13:56.288
Following in daddy's footsteps,
you want to make a deal.

00:13:57.589 --> 00:13:59.788
Little Sammy back
from the dead, and --

00:14:00.089 --> 00:14:02.089
Let me guess, you're
offering up your own soul?

00:14:02.288 --> 00:14:04.889
There are a hundred other demons
who'd love to get their hands on it.

00:14:05.589 --> 00:14:06.989
And it's all yours.

00:14:07.089 --> 00:14:08.788
All you got to do is bring Sam back.

00:14:09.089 --> 00:14:10.288
Give me 10 years.

00:14:11.189 --> 00:14:13.288
10 years, and then you come for me.

00:14:13.389 --> 00:14:14.589
You must be joking.

00:14:16.489 --> 00:14:18.089
That's the same deal.You
give everybody else.

00:14:18.189 --> 00:14:19.788
You're not everybody else.

00:14:23.889 --> 00:14:26.288
Why would I want to give you anything?

00:14:27.788 --> 00:14:30.489
Just keep your gutter soul.
It's too tarnished, anyways.

00:14:32.788 --> 00:14:33.589
Nine years.

00:14:33.689 --> 00:14:34.389
No.

00:14:36.489 --> 00:14:37.089
Eight.

00:14:37.788 --> 00:14:39.589
You keep going, I'll keep saying no.

00:14:41.489 --> 00:14:42.989
Okay, five years.

00:14:44.288 --> 00:14:46.288
Five years, and my bill comes due.

00:14:46.389 --> 00:14:48.689
That's my last offer --
Five years or no deal.

00:14:55.989 --> 00:14:57.189
Then no deal.

00:15:00.389 --> 00:15:02.189
Fine. Fine

00:15:05.089 --> 00:15:07.788
Make sure you bury Sam before
he starts stinking up the joint.

00:15:09.689 --> 00:15:10.489
Wait.

00:15:11.889 --> 00:15:14.389
It's a fire sale, and
everything must go.

00:15:18.788 --> 00:15:19.788
What do I have to do?

00:15:20.989 --> 00:15:22.689
First of all, quit groveling.

00:15:22.889 --> 00:15:24.589
Needy guys are such a turnoff.

00:15:28.589 --> 00:15:29.389
Look...

00:15:30.788 --> 00:15:33.589
I shouldn't be doing this. I
could get in a lot of trouble.

00:15:33.788 --> 00:15:36.288
But what can I say? I got
a blind spot for you, Dean.

00:15:36.989 --> 00:15:40.989
You're like a...puppy. You're
just too fun to play with.

00:15:44.389 --> 00:15:45.288
I'll do it.

00:15:45.889 --> 00:15:46.788
You'll bring him back?

00:15:47.089 --> 00:15:47.889
I will.

00:15:49.189 --> 00:15:50.489
And because I'm such a saint,

00:15:50.589 --> 00:15:53.788
I'll give you one
year and one year only.

00:15:56.989 --> 00:15:57.989
But here's the thing.

00:15:59.389 --> 00:16:02.788
If you try and welch or weasel
your way out, then the deal is off.

00:16:02.989 --> 00:16:05.689
Sam drops dead. He's back
to rotten meat in no time.

00:16:08.089 --> 00:16:08.889
So...

00:16:10.288 --> 00:16:12.288
Its a better deal
than your dad ever got.

00:16:14.788 --> 00:16:15.889
What do you say?

00:16:58.589 --> 00:16:59.389
Sammy.

00:17:00.489 --> 00:17:01.288
Thank god

00:17:01.389 --> 00:17:02.189
Hey.

00:17:07.588 --> 00:17:08.588
Ow.

00:17:08.788 --> 00:17:09.689
Uh, Dean...

00:17:10.389 --> 00:17:11.989
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, man.

00:17:12.088 --> 00:17:13.088
I'm just...

00:17:13.389 --> 00:17:15.288
I'm just happy to see you
up and around, that's all.

00:17:17.389 --> 00:17:18.989
Come on. Sit down. Okay.

00:17:19.588 --> 00:17:22.189
Dean... what happened to me?

00:17:23.489 --> 00:17:24.788
Well, what do you remember?

00:17:25.189 --> 00:17:27.788
I-I saw you and Bobby, and...

00:17:28.989 --> 00:17:31.889
I felt this pain,
this sharp pain like...

00:17:31.989 --> 00:17:33.788
Like, white-Hot, you know, and...

00:17:33.989 --> 00:17:36.088
Then you started running at me, and...

00:17:36.588 --> 00:17:37.588
That's about it.

00:17:38.189 --> 00:17:40.689
Yeah, that -- That kid
stabbed you in the back.

00:17:41.989 --> 00:17:44.889
You lost a lot of blood. It
was touch and go for a while.

00:17:44.989 --> 00:17:47.389
But, Dean, you -- You can't
patch up a wound that bad.

00:17:48.389 --> 00:17:49.489
No, Bobby could.

00:17:51.588 --> 00:17:52.889
Who was that kid,anyway?

00:17:52.989 --> 00:17:54.489
His name's Jake. Did you get him?

00:17:54.588 --> 00:17:56.189
No, he disappeared into the woods.

00:17:56.389 --> 00:17:57.689
We got to find him, Dean.

00:17:58.189 --> 00:18:00.288
And I swear I'm gonna tear
that son of a bitch apart.

00:18:00.389 --> 00:18:02.389
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Easy, van damme.

00:18:03.588 --> 00:18:04.588
You just woke up,all right?

00:18:04.689 --> 00:18:06.788
Let's get you something to
eat. You want something to eat?

00:18:07.788 --> 00:18:09.288
I'm starving. Come on.

00:18:09.588 --> 00:18:11.088
And that's when you guys showed up.

00:18:11.889 --> 00:18:12.989
That's awful.

00:18:13.989 --> 00:18:14.889
Poor Andy.

00:18:16.689 --> 00:18:19.189
The demon said he only wanted
one of us to walk out alive.

00:18:19.389 --> 00:18:20.989
He told you that? Yep.

00:18:22.489 --> 00:18:23.588
He appeared in a dream.

00:18:23.788 --> 00:18:24.989
He tell you anything else?

00:18:27.288 --> 00:18:28.588
No. No.

00:18:28.889 --> 00:18:30.288
That was it. Nothing else.

00:18:31.788 --> 00:18:32.788
You know, what I don't get, Dean,

00:18:32.788 --> 00:18:34.689
Is if the demon only wanted one of us,

00:18:34.788 --> 00:18:36.489
Then how did Jake and I both get away?

00:18:37.788 --> 00:18:39.288
Well, I mean, they left you for dead.

00:18:39.588 --> 00:18:40.788
I'm sure they thought it was over.

00:18:44.889 --> 00:18:47.189
Now that yellow eyes has Jake,
what's he gonna do with him?

00:18:49.389 --> 00:18:50.389
I don't know.

00:18:51.288 --> 00:18:53.088
But whatever it is, we got to stop him.

00:18:53.389 --> 00:18:56.088
Hold on, all right? You
need to get your rest.

00:18:56.189 --> 00:18:57.088
We got time.

00:18:57.189 --> 00:18:58.088
No, we don't.

00:18:58.588 --> 00:19:00.088
Sam, oceans aren't boiling, okay?

00:19:00.189 --> 00:19:01.588
Frogs aren't raining from the sky.

00:19:01.689 --> 00:19:03.489
Let's get you your strength back first.

00:19:05.389 --> 00:19:07.689
Did you call the Roadhouse?
Do they know anything?

00:19:08.389 --> 00:19:09.088
Yeah.

00:19:11.989 --> 00:19:13.889
Dean...what is it?

00:19:19.088 --> 00:19:21.088
The Roadhouse burned to the ground.
Ash is dead, probably Ellen --

00:19:21.189 --> 00:19:22.389
A lot of other hunters, too.

00:19:25.389 --> 00:19:26.189
Demons?

00:19:26.288 --> 00:19:27.389
Yeah, we think so.

00:19:28.088 --> 00:19:29.689
We think because ash found something.

00:19:29.889 --> 00:19:30.788
What'd he find?

00:19:31.189 --> 00:19:32.788
Bobby's working on that right now.

00:19:32.989 --> 00:19:35.389
Well, come on, then. Bobby's
only a few hours away.

00:19:35.689 --> 00:19:38.189
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Stop.
Sam, stop, damn it.

00:19:40.489 --> 00:19:43.389
You almost died in there.
I mean, what would I have --

00:19:45.989 --> 00:19:48.088
You just take care of
yourself for a little bit, huh?

00:19:48.189 --> 00:19:49.288
Just for a little bit.

00:19:50.689 --> 00:19:52.189
I'm sorry. No.

00:20:09.189 --> 00:20:10.989
Hey, Bobby. Hey, Bobby.

00:20:12.088 --> 00:20:13.389
See you up and around.

00:20:13.788 --> 00:20:14.889
Yeah, well...

00:20:15.788 --> 00:20:17.088
Thanks for patching me up.

00:20:18.189 --> 00:20:19.088
Don't mention it.

00:20:25.189 --> 00:20:26.288
Well, Sam's better.

00:20:26.989 --> 00:20:28.489
And we're back in it now, so...

00:20:29.389 --> 00:20:30.389
What do you know?

00:20:35.889 --> 00:20:37.989
Well, I found something,but...

00:20:38.588 --> 00:20:40.588
I'm not sure what the hell it means.

00:20:42.088 --> 00:20:42.989
What is it?

00:20:43.689 --> 00:20:47.588
Demonic omens...like a frickin' tidal
wave. Cattle deaths,lightning storms.

00:20:47.689 --> 00:20:49.389
They skyrocketed from out of nowhere.

00:20:49.489 --> 00:20:50.389
Here.

00:20:52.989 --> 00:20:55.788
All around here
except for one place --

00:20:56.588 --> 00:20:57.788
Southern wyoming.

00:20:57.889 --> 00:20:58.788
Wyoming?

00:20:58.889 --> 00:20:59.489
Yeah.

00:20:59.588 --> 00:21:02.189
That one area's totally
clean -- Spotless.

00:21:02.689 --> 00:21:03.889
It's almost as if...

00:21:04.189 --> 00:21:04.889
What?

00:21:05.288 --> 00:21:07.088
...the demons are surrounding it.

00:21:07.989 --> 00:21:08.689
But you don't know why?

00:21:08.788 --> 00:21:11.288
No, and by this point,
my eyes are swimming.

00:21:12.389 --> 00:21:13.588
Sam, would you take a look at it?

00:21:13.689 --> 00:21:15.538
Maybe you can catch
something I couldn't.

00:21:15.689 --> 00:21:16.689
Yeah, sure.

00:21:18.889 --> 00:21:19.788
Come on, Dean.

00:21:20.389 --> 00:21:22.189
I got some more books in the truck.

00:21:22.689 --> 00:21:23.788
Help me lug them in.

00:21:26.889 --> 00:21:27.588
Yeah.

00:21:34.288 --> 00:21:36.689
You stupid ass! What did you do?

00:21:37.588 --> 00:21:38.989
What did you do?!

00:21:41.588 --> 00:21:44.088
You made a deal... for Sam, didn't you?

00:21:45.588 --> 00:21:46.689
How long did they give you?

00:21:46.989 --> 00:21:47.588
Bobby.

00:21:47.689 --> 00:21:48.889
How long?!

00:21:53.189 --> 00:21:54.189
One year.

00:21:54.889 --> 00:21:56.588
Damn it, Dean.

00:21:57.288 --> 00:21:59.989
Which is why we got to find
this yellow-Eyed son of a bitch.

00:22:01.389 --> 00:22:04.689
That's why I'm gonna kill him myself.
I got nothing to lose now,right?

00:22:05.288 --> 00:22:07.189
I could throttle you!

00:22:07.288 --> 00:22:09.389
And send me downstairsahead of schedule?

00:22:14.489 --> 00:22:16.588
What is it with you Winchesters, huh?

00:22:16.989 --> 00:22:18.189
You, your dad,

00:22:18.288 --> 00:22:21.689
You're both just itching to
throw yourselves down the pit.

00:22:21.889 --> 00:22:22.788
That's my point.

00:22:23.288 --> 00:22:26.439
Dad brought me back, Bobby. I'm
not even supposed to be here.

00:22:27.189 --> 00:22:30.588
At least this way,something good
could come out of it, you know?

00:22:30.889 --> 00:22:31.889
It's like my life can mean something.

00:22:31.989 --> 00:22:34.389
What? And it didn't before?

00:22:34.889 --> 00:22:37.288
Have you got that low
an opinion of yourself?

00:22:37.389 --> 00:22:39.189
Are you that screwed in the head?!

00:22:43.088 --> 00:22:44.889
I couldn't let him die, Bobby.

00:22:46.588 --> 00:22:47.489
I couldn't.

00:22:48.889 --> 00:22:49.989
He's my brother.

00:22:51.689 --> 00:22:53.889
How is your brother gonna feel

00:22:53.989 --> 00:22:56.288
When he knows you're going to hell?

00:22:57.588 --> 00:23:01.088
How'd you feel when you
knew your dad went for you?

00:23:02.588 --> 00:23:03.788
You can't tell him.

00:23:04.689 --> 00:23:06.389
You take a shot at me,
whatever you got to do,

00:23:06.489 --> 00:23:07.788
But please don't tell him.

00:23:28.989 --> 00:23:29.788
Ellen?

00:23:30.588 --> 00:23:31.989
Ellen. Oh, god.

00:23:43.788 --> 00:23:45.489
Bobby, is this really necessary?

00:23:45.588 --> 00:23:48.389
Just a belt of holy
water. Shouldn't hurt.

00:23:54.989 --> 00:23:56.989
Whiskey now, if you don't mind.

00:24:00.189 --> 00:24:01.889
Ellen, what happened? How'd you get out?

00:24:01.989 --> 00:24:03.189
I wasn't supposed to.

00:24:03.288 --> 00:24:05.189
I was supposed to be in
there with everybody else.

00:24:06.788 --> 00:24:09.588
But we ran out of
pretzels, of all things.

00:24:10.489 --> 00:24:11.788
It was just dumb luck.

00:24:17.788 --> 00:24:20.588
Anyway, that's when ash
called, panic in his voice.

00:24:21.788 --> 00:24:23.288
He told me to look in the safe.

00:24:23.689 --> 00:24:24.689
Then the call cut out.

00:24:24.788 --> 00:24:28.189
By the time I got back,
the flames were sky-High,

00:24:29.088 --> 00:24:30.288
And everybody was dead.

00:24:30.389 --> 00:24:32.588
I could n't have been
gone more than 15 minutes.

00:24:34.189 --> 00:24:35.288
Sorry, Ellen.

00:24:35.889 --> 00:24:37.689
A lot of good people died in there.

00:24:38.889 --> 00:24:40.189
And I got to live.

00:24:41.989 --> 00:24:42.889
Lucky me.

00:24:46.088 --> 00:24:47.788
Ellen,you mentioned a safe.

00:24:47.889 --> 00:24:49.288
A hidden safe we keep in the basement.

00:24:49.389 --> 00:24:50.989
Demons get what was in it?

00:24:51.189 --> 00:24:51.788
No.

00:25:00.489 --> 00:25:01.588
Wyoming.

00:25:02.189 --> 00:25:02.989
What does that mean?

00:25:06.889 --> 00:25:07.889
I don't believe it.

00:25:10.588 --> 00:25:11.588
What? You got something?

00:25:12.088 --> 00:25:13.288
A lot more than that.

00:25:15.189 --> 00:25:18.588
Each of these x's is an
abandoned frontier church --

00:25:18.689 --> 00:25:20.588
All mid-19th century

00:25:20.788 --> 00:25:23.489
And all of them built by Samuel Colt.

00:25:23.588 --> 00:25:26.588
Samuel Colt --The demon-Killing,
gunmaking Samuel Colt?

00:25:26.788 --> 00:25:28.889
Yep. And there's more.

00:25:29.389 --> 00:25:31.588
He built private railway lines

00:25:31.989 --> 00:25:33.788
Connecting church to church.

00:25:34.389 --> 00:25:38.189
It just happens to lay out like this.

00:25:39.689 --> 00:25:41.389
Tell me that's not what I think it is.

00:25:41.489 --> 00:25:42.889
It's a devil's trap.

00:25:44.088 --> 00:25:46.189
A 100-Square-Mile
devil's trap.

00:25:46.288 --> 00:25:49.588
That's brilliant. Iron
lines demons can't cross.

00:25:49.689 --> 00:25:51.088
I never heard of anything that massive.

00:25:51.189 --> 00:25:52.189
No one has.

00:25:52.288 --> 00:25:55.189
After all these years none of the
lines are broken? It still works?

00:25:56.088 --> 00:25:57.189
Definitely.

00:25:58.088 --> 00:25:58.989
How do you know?

00:25:59.088 --> 00:26:00.788
All those omens Bobby found.

00:26:00.889 --> 00:26:02.989
That means the demons, they must
be circling and they can't get in.

00:26:03.088 --> 00:26:05.489
Yeah, well... they're trying.

00:26:05.689 --> 00:26:06.788
Why? What's inside?

00:26:07.288 --> 00:26:08.389
That's what I've been looking for,

00:26:08.489 --> 00:26:12.489
And, uh, there's nothing except an old
cowboy cemetery right in the middle.

00:26:13.989 --> 00:26:16.088
Well, what's so important
about a cemetery or...

00:26:16.288 --> 00:26:17.689
What's Colt trying to protect?

00:26:18.889 --> 00:26:19.989
Well, unless...

00:26:20.088 --> 00:26:21.189
Unless what?

00:26:22.288 --> 00:26:24.088
What if Colt wasn't trying
to keep the demons out?

00:26:24.189 --> 00:26:25.889
What if he was trying
to keep something in?

00:26:26.088 --> 00:26:28.588
That's a comforting
thought. Yeah, you think?

00:26:28.689 --> 00:26:30.389
Could they do it, Bobby?
Could they get inside?

00:26:30.489 --> 00:26:31.489
This thing's so powerful,

00:26:31.588 --> 00:26:34.288
You'd practically need
an a-Bomb to destroy it.

00:26:34.389 --> 00:26:36.389
No way a full-Blood demon gets across.

00:26:38.889 --> 00:26:39.788
No.

00:26:41.389 --> 00:26:42.588
But I know who could.

00:27:14.588 --> 00:27:15.489
Howdy, Jake.

00:27:18.588 --> 00:27:19.889
So, did you have a nice trip?

00:27:20.088 --> 00:27:20.989
I'm here.

00:27:21.189 --> 00:27:23.088
I did what you asked. Now what?

00:27:23.689 --> 00:27:27.088
50 miles thataway, there's
a cemetery, a crypt.

00:27:27.189 --> 00:27:28.588
You got to open that for me.

00:27:28.989 --> 00:27:30.489
Think you can manage that, sport?

00:27:30.689 --> 00:27:32.788
You know what? Screw you
and your freaky orders.

00:27:32.889 --> 00:27:33.788
Go do it yourself.

00:27:33.889 --> 00:27:36.788
Oh, I can't. I can't
go that way -- Not yet.

00:27:36.889 --> 00:27:37.889
Why not?

00:27:40.389 --> 00:27:41.989
I just can't.

00:27:42.389 --> 00:27:45.788
But if you're gonna open that crypt
for me, you're gonna need a key.

00:27:46.288 --> 00:27:47.189
A gun?

00:27:47.288 --> 00:27:49.588
Oh, this isn't just any gun, Jake.

00:27:49.788 --> 00:27:52.788
This is the only gun
in the whole universe

00:27:52.889 --> 00:27:54.788
That can shoot me dead.

00:27:55.889 --> 00:27:57.288
Is that so? Yep.

00:27:57.788 --> 00:27:58.889
Here, take it.

00:28:04.788 --> 00:28:05.689
Oh, my.

00:28:05.889 --> 00:28:08.989
I'm shocked at this
unforeseen turn of events.

00:28:09.088 --> 00:28:11.788
Go ahead, Jake.Squeeze that
trigger. Be all you can be.

00:28:11.889 --> 00:28:14.189
This will all be over. Your
life can go back to normal.

00:28:14.689 --> 00:28:16.788
Of course, the army won't take
you back 'cause you're awol.

00:28:16.889 --> 00:28:20.389
But I'm sure you could get your
old job at the factory back.

00:28:21.489 --> 00:28:22.689
But then, on the other hand,

00:28:22.788 --> 00:28:25.689
The rest of your life and your family's

00:28:25.788 --> 00:28:28.689
Could be money and
honey, health and wealth,

00:28:28.788 --> 00:28:30.989
Every day is ice-Cream sundae.

00:28:31.088 --> 00:28:33.088
And all you got to do
is this one little thing.

00:28:33.189 --> 00:28:34.088
Why me?

00:28:34.189 --> 00:28:37.288
Oh, Jake. It's got to be you.

00:28:37.689 --> 00:28:40.889
I've been waiting for
you for a very long time.

00:28:41.189 --> 00:28:42.088
You're my leader.

00:28:42.189 --> 00:28:44.889
You open that crypt, and
you will have your army.

00:28:44.989 --> 00:28:46.689
You're talking about
the end of the world.

00:28:46.788 --> 00:28:49.389
No, not the end
-- The beginning...

00:28:49.788 --> 00:28:52.588
A better world where your
family will be protected.

00:28:52.689 --> 00:28:53.989
More than that.

00:28:54.889 --> 00:28:56.189
They'll be royalty.

00:28:58.288 --> 00:29:00.088
Buddy boy,you have the chance

00:29:00.189 --> 00:29:03.088
To get in on the ground floor
of a thrilling opportunity.

00:29:03.189 --> 00:29:04.288
What do you say?

00:29:04.489 --> 00:29:05.489
It's your call.

00:29:17.788 --> 00:29:18.889
Attababy.

00:29:45.489 --> 00:29:46.489
Howdy, Jake.

00:29:57.989 --> 00:29:58.989
Wait...

00:29:59.489 --> 00:30:01.689
You were dead.I killed you. Yeah?

00:30:02.588 --> 00:30:03.889
Well, next time, finish the job.

00:30:03.989 --> 00:30:05.088
I did.

00:30:05.989 --> 00:30:08.288
I cut clean through
your spinal cord, man.

00:30:12.489 --> 00:30:14.088
You can't be alive.

00:30:16.189 --> 00:30:17.288
You can't be.

00:30:17.588 --> 00:30:20.489
Okay, just take it real easy there, son.

00:30:20.889 --> 00:30:21.889
And if I don't?

00:30:21.989 --> 00:30:23.189
Wait and see.

00:30:24.788 --> 00:30:26.489
What, you a tough guy all of a sudden?

00:30:27.189 --> 00:30:28.788
What are you gonna
do -- Kill me?

00:30:28.989 --> 00:30:29.889
It's a thought.

00:30:29.989 --> 00:30:31.989
You had your chance. You couldn't.

00:30:32.288 --> 00:30:33.989
I won't make that mistake twice.

00:30:38.588 --> 00:30:40.389
What are you smiling
at, you little bitch?

00:30:43.088 --> 00:30:43.989
Hey, lady.

00:30:45.689 --> 00:30:46.689
Do me a favor.

00:30:48.288 --> 00:30:49.889
Put that gun to your head.

00:31:01.389 --> 00:31:02.689
See, that ava girl was right.

00:31:02.788 --> 00:31:03.689
Once you give in to it,

00:31:03.788 --> 00:31:06.689
There's all sorts of new jedi
mind tricks you can learn.

00:31:06.788 --> 00:31:07.788
Let her go.

00:31:08.088 --> 00:31:09.588
Shoot him.

00:31:10.088 --> 00:31:12.088
You'll be mopping up skull
before you get a shot off.

00:31:14.889 --> 00:31:17.189
Everybody, put your guns down.

00:31:19.288 --> 00:31:20.689
Except you, sweetheart.

00:31:39.788 --> 00:31:40.689
Okay.

00:31:41.189 --> 00:31:41.989
Thank you.

00:32:11.788 --> 00:32:14.389
Please...don't.

00:32:15.088 --> 00:32:16.088
Please.

00:32:48.389 --> 00:32:49.189
Oh, no.

00:32:49.489 --> 00:32:50.389
Bobby, what is it?

00:32:51.689 --> 00:32:52.689
It's hell.

00:32:55.389 --> 00:32:56.489
Take cover
-- Now!

00:33:18.288 --> 00:33:18.989
What the hell just happened?!

00:33:19.088 --> 00:33:22.088
That's a devil's gate,
a damn door to hell!

00:33:30.189 --> 00:33:31.989
Come on! We got to shut that gate!

00:33:42.088 --> 00:33:43.588
If the demon gave this to Jake...

00:33:44.989 --> 00:33:45.889
Then maybe...

00:33:53.689 --> 00:33:55.288
A boy shouldn't play with daddy's guns.

00:34:12.088 --> 00:34:13.088
Dean!

00:34:19.689 --> 00:34:21.288
I'll get to you in a minute, champ.

00:34:21.588 --> 00:34:23.989
I'm proud of you --
Knew you had it in you.

00:34:30.989 --> 00:34:31.989
Sit a spell.

00:34:36.788 --> 00:34:38.389
So, Dean...

00:34:38.788 --> 00:34:40.389
I got to thank you.

00:34:40.588 --> 00:34:43.288
You see, demons can't resurrect people

00:34:43.389 --> 00:34:44.689
Unless a deal is made.

00:34:44.788 --> 00:34:47.288
I know, red tape --
It'll make you nuts.

00:34:47.389 --> 00:34:51.088
But thanks to you,
Sammy's back in rotation.

00:34:51.989 --> 00:34:54.288
Now, I wasn't counting
on that, but I'm glad.

00:34:54.389 --> 00:34:56.389
I liked him better than Jake, anyhow.

00:34:58.189 --> 00:34:59.088
Tell
me --

00:34:59.189 --> 00:35:00.088
Have you ever heard the expression

00:35:00.189 --> 00:35:03.489
"If a deal sounds too good
to be true, it probably is"?

00:35:03.788 --> 00:35:05.489
You call that deal good?

00:35:05.889 --> 00:35:08.189
It's a better shake
than your dad ever got.

00:35:08.689 --> 00:35:11.489
And you never wondered why?

00:35:11.989 --> 00:35:13.389
I'm surprised at you.

00:35:14.189 --> 00:35:14.989
I mean...

00:35:15.788 --> 00:35:18.588
You saw what your brother
just did to Jake, right?

00:35:18.889 --> 00:35:20.989
That was pretty cold,wasn't it?

00:35:23.989 --> 00:35:25.989
How certain are you

00:35:26.088 --> 00:35:30.239
That what you brought
back is 100% pure Sam?

00:35:39.389 --> 00:35:40.887
You of all people should know

00:35:40.889 --> 00:35:43.788
That what's dead should stay dead.

00:35:45.788 --> 00:35:46.588
Anyway...

00:35:48.088 --> 00:35:49.588
Thanks a bunch.

00:35:49.788 --> 00:35:52.288
I knew I kept you alive for some reason.

00:35:52.689 --> 00:35:54.189
Until now, anyway.

00:35:55.889 --> 00:35:56.989
I couldn't have done it

00:35:57.088 --> 00:35:59.189
Without your pathetic, self-Loathing,

00:35:59.288 --> 00:36:01.389
Self-Destructive desire

00:36:01.489 --> 00:36:03.788
To sacrifice yourself for your family.

00:38:48.289 --> 00:38:50.188
Well, check that off the to-Do list.

00:38:51.889 --> 00:38:52.889
You did it.

00:38:53.489 --> 00:38:54.588
I didn't do it alone.

00:38:57.588 --> 00:38:58.989
Do you think dad really...

00:39:00.688 --> 00:39:02.688
Do you think he really
climbed out of hell?

00:39:04.188 --> 00:39:05.588
The door was open.

00:39:09.088 --> 00:39:10.789
If anyone's stubborn enough to do it...

00:39:13.289 --> 00:39:14.289
It would be him.

00:39:19.289 --> 00:39:20.688
Where do you think he is now?

00:39:23.389 --> 00:39:24.389
I don't know.

00:39:27.088 --> 00:39:29.389
I kind of can't believe
it, Dean.I mean...

00:39:30.989 --> 00:39:32.588
Our whole lives,everything...

00:39:33.289 --> 00:39:35.289
Has been prepping for this, and now I...

00:39:39.489 --> 00:39:41.289
I kind of don't know what to say.

00:39:45.088 --> 00:39:45.889
I do.

00:39:55.289 --> 00:39:56.889
That was for our mom...

00:39:59.188 --> 00:40:00.688
You son of a bitch.

00:40:10.389 --> 00:40:11.889
You know, when Jake saw me...

00:40:12.588 --> 00:40:13.989
It was like he saw a ghost.

00:40:18.688 --> 00:40:20.389
I mean, hell, you heard him, Dean.

00:40:21.789 --> 00:40:22.789
He said he killed me.

00:40:25.688 --> 00:40:26.889
I'm glad he was wrong.

00:40:27.289 --> 00:40:28.688
I don't think he was,Dean.

00:40:32.289 --> 00:40:34.989
What happened... after I was stabbed?

00:40:36.889 --> 00:40:38.789
I already told you. Not everything.

00:40:41.188 --> 00:40:42.989
Sam, we just killed the demon.

00:40:44.989 --> 00:40:46.789
Can we celebrate for a minute?

00:40:52.088 --> 00:40:53.289
Did I die?

00:40:53.588 --> 00:40:54.989
Oh, come on.

00:40:55.789 --> 00:40:58.088
Did you sell your soul for
me, like dad did for you?

00:40:58.188 --> 00:40:59.088
Come on! No

00:41:04.289 --> 00:41:05.389
Tell me the truth.

00:41:08.289 --> 00:41:09.588
Dean, tell me the truth.

00:41:09.688 --> 00:41:10.588
Sam...

00:41:21.489 --> 00:41:22.739
How long do you get?

00:41:28.688 --> 00:41:29.688
One year.

00:41:32.289 --> 00:41:33.389
I got one year.

00:41:36.688 --> 00:41:37.989
You shouldn't have done that.

00:41:39.088 --> 00:41:40.088
How could you do that?

00:41:40.188 --> 00:41:41.289
Don't get mad at me.

00:41:43.688 --> 00:41:44.688
Don't you do that.

00:41:46.989 --> 00:41:47.989
I had to.

00:41:49.188 --> 00:41:50.688
I had to look out for you.

00:41:52.088 --> 00:41:53.088
That's my job.

00:41:53.188 --> 00:41:54.889
And what do you think my job is?

00:41:55.389 --> 00:41:56.088
What?

00:41:56.489 --> 00:41:59.688
You saved my life over and over.

00:42:00.289 --> 00:42:01.588
I mean, you sacrifice everything for me.

00:42:01.688 --> 00:42:03.389
Don't you think I'd do the same for you?

00:42:06.588 --> 00:42:07.489
You're my big brother.

00:42:08.588 --> 00:42:11.688
There's nothing I wouldn't do for you.

00:42:15.889 --> 00:42:18.289
And I don't care what it takes.
I'm gonna get you out of this.

00:42:21.989 --> 00:42:24.088
Guess I got to save
your ass for a change.

00:42:25.889 --> 00:42:26.489
Yeah.

00:42:27.989 --> 00:42:28.789
Well...

00:42:29.889 --> 00:42:31.688
Yellow-Eyed demon might be dead,

00:42:31.989 --> 00:42:33.789
But a lot more got through that gate.

00:42:33.989 --> 00:42:34.989
How many, you think?

00:42:35.588 --> 00:42:38.188
100, maybe 200.

00:42:38.489 --> 00:42:39.489
It's an army.

00:42:40.989 --> 00:42:42.489
He's unleashed an army.

00:42:45.489 --> 00:42:47.088
Hope to hell you boys are ready.

00:42:47.789 --> 00:42:49.389
'Cause the war has just begun.

00:42:51.889 --> 00:42:52.989
Well, then...

00:43:02.688 --> 00:43:03.989
We got work to do.



00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:08.989
